  "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition, \n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{TS}=\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PS},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/6d9225f220f50031fcbc7680c697b31eb8ce7733f07b83713c0dbe0c2ad89490.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{TP}=-c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/533805fc0d558bde49590a6dd82414de22efeeadbc76e91760bea33bcd0ceeff.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TS} & =\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PS} \\\\  & =-c+a \\\\  & =a-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
